==== Installation with CFE HTTP gui  ====

  - Switch off the router
  - Plug an ethernet cable into any LAN port and connect the other end to a computer.  
  - Use a pen or paperclip to press and //hold// the **RESET** button on the back.  
  - While holding down the RESET button, turn the power switch on and wait ~6 seconds until the power light comes on (solid red).  Then release the RESET button. 
  - On your computer, configure your ethernet settings to "static IP".  Set the address to ''192.168.1.2'' and the netmask to ''255.255.255.0'' AKA ''/24''.  Set the gateway to ''192.168.1.1''.  
  - Be sure to disconnect the computer from wifi or any network that uses the ''192.168.1.1/24'' subnet.  
  - Open a browser and go to http://192.168.1.1/  You should see a page asking you to get an image from your ISP.  
  - Upload the new firmware image and wait.  After a few seconds the screen will say "New software is being programmed to the flash memory..."  After a few minutes it will reboot and the web page will disconnect.  
  - Now you can switch the ethernet connection settings on your computer from "static IP" to "DHCP client" and try to reconnect to http://192.168.1.1/.  This time it should be the luci web console for the newly installed OpenWrt.  

